            <ArticleTitle>Waging the War on Clinical Grade Inflation: The Ongoing Quest.</ArticleTitle>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1097/NNE.0000000000000473</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>This study examined the presence of grade inflation in clinical courses 9 years after implementing strategies to improve grading precision. A comparison of clinical grades for cohort I (1997-2002) with cohort II (2009-2016) showed statistically lower grades in 2 courses (Adult 1 and Maternity) for cohort II. Suggestions for changing the way clinical experiences are planned, executed, and evaluated are provided.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
